  "description": "DARROF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H48 Dy4 N24 O18. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.732-4.278 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.95-125.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C52H48Dy4N24O18. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
